    "title": "pandas.errors.PossiblePrecisionLoss — pandas 3.1.0.dev0 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.errors.PossiblePrecisionLoss#\n\n- exception pandas.errors.PossiblePrecisionLoss[source]#\n- Warning raised by to_stata on a column with a value outside or equal to int64. When the column value is outside or equal to the int64 value the column is converted to a float64 dtype. See also \n  - `DataFrame.to_stata`\n  - Export DataFrame object to Stata dta format.\n Examples >>> df = pd.DataFrame({\"s\": pd.Series([1, 2**53], dtype=np.int64)}) >>> df.to_stata(\"test\")",
